  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The lily is a single HDA and a single Copernicus trim sheet. Its six maps (height, base colour, normal, ambient occlusion, roughness and opacity) come from a graph of stock Houdini nodes: no VEX, no wrangle, and no image file read inside the graph. The shots are rendered in Unreal Engine 5.8 with Lumen. It took two days, 5 and 6 October 2026. Claude Code, Codex and Gemini built and checked things while I set the rules and validated every step.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
