  {
   "id": "brief",
   "type": "heading",
   "props": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The brief and the rules",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On 5 October I opened a new project called ZenRay Vegetation Collection 01. The plan was three vegetation assets in the same Houdini scene, each one after a different post by Erwan Gaudichon: a ",
     "styles": {}
    },
    {
     "type": "link",
     "href": "https://www.artstation.com/artwork/VyE3V4",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "lily",
       "styles": {}
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": ", a ",
     "styles": {}
    },
    {
     "type": "link",
     "href": "https://www.artstation.com/artwork/a0gxvk",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "pampas grass",
       "styles": {}
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " and a ",
     "styles": {}
    },
    {
     "type": "link",
     "href": "https://www.artstation.com/artwork/5WVB5w",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "eucalyptus",
       "styles": {}
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": ". I downloaded the 23 images of the three posts in 4K and cut them into reference sheets: material crops and component sheets. The four-view sheets and the reference height maps were generated from them with an image generator.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The lily came first because it was the simplest, and it is the only asset that was finished at the end of the second day. The pampas grass stays at a first model of about 9,000 polygons. The eucalyptus attempts, a trunk built with a Point VOP and a canopy of hanging clusters, never reached the reference, so I archived the last version and stopped. Both are still on the list.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "props": {
    "level": 3
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "How I work with agents",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Three agents worked on this project: Claude Code, Codex and Gemini. They do not share a conversation, they share a memory. ZenRay Assets V2 maps every folder of the project (the workshop, the Houdini scene, the Unreal content, the notes), keeps a feedback file with every prompt and every correction, and writes a checkpoint at the end of each session. Houdini is driven live through a small bridge, Unreal through a queue of Python scripts.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "props": {
    "columns": [
     "Agent",
     "What it did on this project"
    ],
    "rows": [
     [
      "Claude Code",
      "The lily HDA, the Copernicus graph and its six maps, the look development in Houdini, the Unreal level, the cameras, the renders, the two 2048 px cuts, the audio and the covers."
     ],
     [
      "Codex",
      "The first eucalyptus attempts, the base colour and occlusion pass on band 0, the title animations and the Vogun weights, the Cycles and Octane research and install, the completed evolution videos, the numbered steps and the 4096 px video."
     ],
     [
      "Gemini",
      "The first height evolution video, assembled from 77 states."
     ]
    ],
    "caption": "Who did what. I set the rules, chose, and validated."
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "That only works with rules, and most of them came from mistakes made in the first hours:",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "A reference is measured, never copied.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " Masks, profiles and tables are allowed. A reference image that a node reads, resizes, blends or traces is not.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Image generation is mine.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " The agents never generate images. I can give them an image as a reference, never as a result.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Real nodes only in Copernicus.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " No VEX, no wrangle, no Python inside a graph. Python builds the graph and measures it, the nodes carry the shape.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "One band at a time.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " A band is finished, or declared provisional, before the next one opens, and I validate it.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Iterate by blocks.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " A block of up to 64 nodes to explore, then an optimisation pass that removes what does not matter.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Every iteration leaves an image,",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " in a folder called versions, before the next one starts.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Seamless by construction.",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " A whole number of cells and a Wrap border, never a cut that is glued afterwards.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "At most eight parameters per folder",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " on an HDA. The rest stays inside the network.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "bulletListItem",
   "props": {},
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Never rebuild what I tuned by hand,",
     "styles": {
      "bold": true
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " a light, a camera, a material value, without asking.",
     "styles": {}
    }
   ]
  },
