     "type": "text",
     "text": "For one band the loop is always the same. Pick one representative cell of the reference, never an average. Measure its contour as a curve, with a mirror when the organ is symmetric. Draw that contour with nodes. Get the volume from the distance to the edge and a profile curve. Get veins and fibres from direction fields. Repeat the cell a whole number of times with a controlled variation per cell. Then compare side by side and with numbers, and only then add the next block of nodes.",
