     "type": "text",
     "text": "The colour came only once the height was good, and it comes from the height: the base colour is derived from it, with palettes measured on reference photos. The first petal colour was wrong in an instructive way. I coloured the petal by its height, but in a real petal the colour depends on the distance to the edge: the edge is almost white, and the colour builds up towards the inside, deeper in the middle. A photo made that clear. The petal colour is now driven by the distance to the contour: about one per cent of the sheet width of clean white, then a short transition into the colour.",
